th g7 and he just waits  and now my my rook or king have to move  and i'm essentially in some sort of zulu  vong  um but it's going to be losing  regardless for white decide to play king  to c1 then he plays rook d4 i don't have  king c3 to attack the rook and he's  building the bridge like this  i play king c2  king e2  and yeah if i give a check he's ready to  do this this and again this is a bridge  king is sheltered pawn is queening  so i didn't resign here because i had  one last trick up my sleeve  after king c3 he plays rook f4  i play rook to b5  with a very deep idea  that after he queens  i play rook to b1  we got this position  and i said oh no my rook  although i didn't say oh no my rook but  i i said it to myself  and i tried to  hide my laughter in this position and of  course he does not take it  but he plays queen c6 or queen f3 and i  resign  um  for the the beginners watching who are  maybe confused if he were to take my  rook this would be stalemate so  had to get in at least one stalemate  trap this tournament but uh yeah it's  not going to work against a strong gm  so it's a tough game um  i have a feeling i know where things  went wrong if we go back  uh  i'll very quickly look at the engine  but  i also kind of want food so let's just  look at this moment  uh oh both moves are playable okay  uh but yeah already here it's it's  tricky i should have played rook h8  it's interesting engines giving a small  plus to light  should still be a draw though  so what was my losing move  ah rook d6 yeah  i was in time trouble  so engine says i should take  but it's super unpleasant to defend this  anyway yeah it was tough game  uh kudos to my opponents  i hope people learned a thing or two  from this fight maybe we're somewhat  entertained  so thanks for watching if you made it  this far  and now it's time for food
 

